  "notes": "Parameter keys other than classuri/querymode are connector jargon the prompt does not name (models write queryMode, vertexLabel, strip-uri-prefixes ...), so graph labels, rdf-type, URI stripping and the Gremlin/SPARQL query are matched on the Parameters map text. The prompt does not give the exact Gremlin query or the URI strings, so only its structure (a g.V() or g.E() traversal, limit(10), source/destination/code/route) and the air-routes namespaces are checked. The prompt attaches the query to the LPG tables as a group, not to customairport, so any LPG table may carry it; real outputs put it on route or airport. Graph labels are tested as any parameter text naming vertex, edge or view. 'The same columns' is tested as shared column names plus the same type families; comparing the whole column list wrongly failed a real output whose columns differ only in a Comment, and the schema cannot compare two name sets exactly."
